#reason src/renderer/lib/lanternguidenote.ts A reviewer needs the step's title and why next to the file's diff, not in a separate view, to know what to look for.
#reason src/renderer/lantern-guide.css Styles the left-pane guide, the step note and the marked diff lines in place of the old full-screen Guide view.
#reason src/renderer/lantern-select.css The step's why above a diff is readable text like the reason row, so it must stay selectable.
#reason src/renderer/lantern.css The full-screen Guide host no longer exists, so its diff colour scope is dropped.
#reason src/renderer/lib/lanternguide.ts Reviewers walk a guided PR file by file, so the guide has to become an ordered list of stops and line marks instead of a set of hunks to scroll.
#reason src/renderer/lib/lanternguideview.ts The steps now replace the file list in the left pane, so the pane lists each step's files and highlights the current one instead of drawing hunks.
#reason src/renderer/lib/lanternmacroview.ts The guide no longer needs a view switch, so the strip goes back to Files, Macro and Flow.
#reason src/renderer/lib/lanternprpanel.ts With the Guide button gone, a guide that could not be read would be invisible, so the header carries a note and the flow strip stays with the guide pane.
#reason src/renderer/lib/lanternreview.ts The review pane is where the diff is read, so it shows the step note and marks the lines the step names, and repaints when only the step changes.
#reason src/renderer/lib/lanternview.ts The guide belongs to the existing review flow, so the file list, review order and arrow stepping follow guide order and the Guide view is removed.
#reason src/renderer/lib/prdiffmodal.ts Marking the step's lines must happen after the async diff is drawn, so the diff view now tells its owner when it has filled.
#reason test/e2e/pr-review-guide.spec.ts Proves in the real app that the guide is in the left pane, one file's diff is in the middle, arrow keys follow guide order and Flow stays available.
#reason test/lantern-guide-view.test.ts Pins the stop order, the marking and the guide pane, and that the review screen shows the guide without a Guide button and still works without one.
#story A reviewer reads a guided pull request file by file
#step actor Reviewer
#step action opens a pull request that has a guide
